(Bug #110: a single-quoted ONE-WORD name must resolve inside a `{...}`
 format-string slot exactly as it does everywhere else - LANGUAGE.md:711
 rule 4, a single-word quoted identifier "lexes identically to the bare
 form". Before the fix, `try_parse_expression`'s no-space guard (it only
 looked for a space to decide whether content might be an expression)
 treated `'tally'` as plain unparsed text, and the slot parser stored the
 raw quoted string - quote marks included - as the variable name, so it
 never matched the `tally` the rest of the compiler declared it under:
 `Print "{'tally'}".` failed with "Unknown variable: 'tally'" even though
 `Print 'tally'.` printed 7 just fine.)

a number called 'tally' is 7.
Print 'tally'.
Print "{'tally'}".
